course: dictionary
lesson: 11424
title: Acquire: getting and learning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Acquire is a formal word. It means to get or gain something, by buying it, being given it or working for it. «Mia acquired a new bike for her birthday.» She got the bike, so acquire means get.
explain: You can also acquire a skill, a habit or knowledge by learning it over time. «Sam is acquiring good reading skills.» He is learning them bit by bit. Children acquire words the same way, by hearing and using them.
explain: Look at the context to see which meaning fits. Ask: has something been gained, bought or learned? Then swap in the word get or learn to check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Acquire means to get or gain something.
fact: Acquire can also mean to learn or develop a skill, habit or knowledge.
fact: Acquire is a formal word, so you will often meet it in books and important writing.
fact: In business, to acquire a company means to buy it.
fact: The noun from acquire is acquisition, meaning something that has been gained.
exercise: «Ben acquires 8 more marbles.» Which sum shows what happens to his marbles? | *Add 8 | Take away 8 | Multiply by 8 | Divide by 8
exercise: «Sara acquired a taste for spicy food.» What does this mean? | She cooked spicy food for her friends | She threw her spicy food away | She hated spicy food | *She came to enjoy spicy food
exercise: Lee wants to acquire knowledge about volcanoes. What is he trying to do? | Forget everything about volcanoes | Paint a picture of a volcano | Buy a real volcano | *Learn about volcanoes
test: «The company plans to acquire a smaller rival.» What does acquire mean in this business sentence? | *To buy the other company | To move to a new town | To sell its shops | To close the office
test: «Children acquire new words every day by reading and listening.» What does acquire mean here? | To throw away | To lose | To shout loudly | *To learn or pick up
exam: Which word is the noun form of acquire? | *acquisition | acquaintance | acquittal | acquired
